  "ReactData": {
    "AddToOrderMarkup": null,
    "Copies": [
      "<span class=\"Wrd\">Our most</span> popular hex head <span class=\"Wrd\">screws.</span> These have a head with six flat sides to keep wrenches and sockets from slipping and rounding off the <span class=\"Wrd\">drive.</span> ",
      "Length is measured from under the <span class=\"Wrd\">head.</span>",
      "<b>High</b><b>-</b><b>Strength</b> <span class=\"Wrd\"><b>Fastener</b><b>—</b></span>Commonly used to fasten components in <span class=\"Wrd\">valves,</span> <span class=\"Wrd\">pumps,</span> <span class=\"Wrd\">motors,</span> and other high-stress <span class=\"Wrd\">applications.</span> These screws have a tensile strength of <span class=\"Wrd\">125,</span>000 to <span class=\"Wrd\">160,</span>000 <span class=\"Wrd\">psi.</span>",
      "<b>Zinc</b><b>-</b><b>Yellow</b><b>-</b><b>Chromate</b><b>-</b><b>Plated</b> <span class=\"Wrd\"><b>Steel</b><b>—</b></span>With slightly better corrosion resistance than zinc-plated steel <span class=\"Wrd\">screws,</span> these stand up to more frequent exposure to <span class=\"Wrd\">moisture.</span>"
    ],
    "Headers": {
      "Primary": "High-Strength Zinc Yellow-Chromate Plated Hex Head Screw",
      "Secondary": "Grade 8 Steel, 3/8\"-16 Thread Size, 1\" Long, Fully Threaded"
    },
